Someone expressed concern about the fact that yogurt only contains one kind
of culture, and that that might not be enough to properly repopulate the
digestive system after taking antibiotics.  Well, at my local health food
store (Country Sun -- YMMV), I found a brand called Mello Bros.  It's
nonfat, fruit-juice sweetened, and comes "with living cultures:  S.
Thermophilus, L. Bulgaricus, L. Acidophilus, and Bifidus".

I have no further data, but those concerned with cultural diversity (so to
speak) may want to try it.

